preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: 1. Ultrabooks and convertible laptops were prominent at CES 2013.\n2. 4K resolution and 3D displays were showcased by several manufacturers.\n3. Smartwatches and fitness trackers were introduced by companies like Sony and Qualcomm.\n4. Smart home automation and IoT devices were displayed by companies like Samsung and LG.\n5. High-speed mobile charging technologies, such as wireless charging pads, were demonstrated.\n6. Curved and flexible displays were showcased by companies like Samsung and LG.'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: At CES 2013, some notable trends included:\n\n1. Ultra High Definition (UHD) TVs\n2. Smartwatches and wearable technology\n3. 3D printing and home manufacturing\n4. Cloud gaming and streaming services\n5. Smart home automation and connected devices\n6. Tablets and mobile devices with larger screens'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: CES 2013 took place from January 8 to January 11, 2013. Here are 6 trends from that event:\n\n1. **Smartwatches and Wearable Technology**: Samsung and Qualcomm showcased their smartwatch concepts, which were some of the first examples of wearable technology that could connect to smartphones.\n\n2. **Ultra HD (4K) Displays**: Several companies, including LG and Sony, demonstrated 4K resolution displays, which offered higher picture quality than traditional HDTVs.\n\n3. **Tablet Computing**: Tablets were a major focus at CES 2013, with many manufacturers showcasing their latest Android and Windows-based tablets, including the Microsoft Surface.\n\n4. **Cloud Gaming**: Cloud gaming services, such as OnLive and Gaikai (later acquired by Sony), were gaining traction, allowing users to play high-end games on lower-powered devices.\n\n5. **Internet-Connected Appliances**: Smart home technology was becoming more mainstream, with companies like Samsung and LG showcasing internet-connected appliances, such as refrigerators and washing machines.\n\n6. **3D Printing**: 3D printing technology was gaining attention at CES 2013, with several companies showcasing their latest 3D printing devices and applications, including printing custom phone cases and jewelry.'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: CES 2013 took place from January 8 to 11, 2013. Here are 6 trends from that event:\n\n1. **Smartwatches and Wearable Technology**: CES 2013 saw the emergence of smartwatches and wearable technology, with companies like Pebble and Samsung showcasing their wearable devices.\n2. **4K and Ultra HD TVs**: The event highlighted the growing trend of 4K and Ultra HD TVs, with several manufacturers showcasing their high-resolution displays.\n3. **Tablet Computing**: Tablets continued to be a major focus at CES 2013, with companies like Microsoft, Sony, and Samsung introducing new tablet models.\n4. **Internet of Things (IoT)**: The concept of the Internet of Things (IoT) gained significant attention at CES 2013, with companies showcasing connected devices and smart home products.\n5. **Smart Home Automation**: Smart home automation was another trend that emerged at CES 2013, with companies like Samsung and LG showcasing their smart home products and services.\n6. **Mobile Payments**: Mobile payments were also a major focus at CES 2013, with companies like Google, PayPal, and Square showcasing their mobile payment solutions.'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meani